--- body ---
## Context
Author ruling, 2026-10-29 (lair session, after closing the fifth hoard #1975 unmerged): rename
hoard. "Dream" is taken; the author chose **smelt** over temper, assay and anneal. Fire turns
ore into metal and leaves the slag behind: journal entries are the ore, topics the metal, stale
claims the slag. The output is smaller than the input, which is the point (ticket 1348's
theory of change; the name "hoard" described the defect, a store that only grows).

## Scope
- Harness: `skills/hoard/` → `skills/smelt/`; `memory/HOARD.md` → `memory/SMELT.md`;
  `memory/hoards/` → `memory/smelts/` (ledger history kept with `git mv`); every reference in
  skills, rules, AGENTS.md, scripts, tests, adapters and the skills catalog (about 55 files
  outside journal, conception and closed tickets, which keep the old word as history).
  Lair step 12's suggestion line follows.
- Consumer projects: each project with memory carries a versioned HOARD.md and `memory/hoards/`.
  One ticket per project repository (cross-project rule), filed when the harness rename lands.
- Description routing: the first sentence states the plain function (`rules/authoring-skills.md`).
- Land before 1349, so the rebuild runs under the new name.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `grep -rniw hoard` outside history paths (journal, conception, closed tickets, hoard reports) finds nothing
- [ ] `make check` and `make check-skills-drift` pass
- [ ] Per-project rename tickets filed in every repository with a memory store

## Imagine (raid 0a53b8)
Premise holds: the author ruled the name; nothing here reopens it. Evidence (git grep, 2026-10-29):
- `git grep -i hoard` outside journal, conception, closed tickets, memory/hoards finds 38 files,
  275 lines. Of these, 73 lines sit in `memory/evidence/2026-10-15-raid-review-evidence.md` and
  1 in `health/journal.jsonl`: both append-only records, history. Live sites: about 28 files.
- Path renames (`-w` misses underscores): `skills/hoard/`, `memory/HOARD.md`, `memory/hoards/`
  (7 reports), `scripts/hoard_migrate.py`, `tests/test_hoard_migrate.py`. The ticket's "about 55
  files" overstates; real blast radius is about 28 edited + 10 renamed paths.
- Installed projection: only `~/.claude/skills/hoard` -> `$IDH_ROOT/skills/hoard` exists
  (absolute symlink, would dangle after merge). No Codex or Pi hoard link found on this host;
  `adapters/projections.json` lists no hoard entry. Refresh: `bin/idh install skill smelt`
  (README), then remove the dangling `hoard` link.
- Alias: not needed. Precedent is the dream->hoard rename (closed 1102-1109): "no managed
  old-name alias" (memory/topics/memory-v8-governance.md). `smelt` does not mislead; a stale
  `/hoard` fails loudly. The one place the old word must live on is detection of historical
  names in corpora (`scripts/census/memory-recall.py`, `scripts/trace-stats.py` list dream and
  hoard as past names) and lair's blob-ledger reading of old `memory/hoards/*.md`.
- Consumer stores found under ~/CNRS (read-only): `projets/actifs/padme` (HOARD.md, versioned);
  `JETP-observer`, `climate-finance-het` and `code/arena/repos/agents`... carry legacy
  `DREAM.md` (never migrated to HOARD.md); `code/DOIfetch` and `code/arena` have memory/ with
  only a journal. So the "every project carries HOARD.md" premise is wrong: one project does.
- Overlap 1347: its text says "hoard input" in 3 lines and its scope touches hoard input
  selection. 1348/1349 also cite `skills/hoard/SKILL.md:69-70`. Order 1352 first (ticket says so);
  1347, 1348, 1349 then rebase and rename their prose to smelt (their tickets are edited in
  this sweep, so only code conflicts remain).

## Plan (raid 0a53b8)
Actions, one mechanical commit (`git mv` first, then sed on the word, then fix case/grammar):
1. `git mv skills/hoard skills/smelt; memory/HOARD.md memory/SMELT.md; memory/hoards memory/smelts;
   scripts/hoard_migrate.py scripts/smelt_migrate.py; tests/test_hoard_migrate.py
   tests/test_smelt_migrate.py`. Also `tests/test_lair_dream_suggestion.py` stays named, content updated.
2. Rewrite frontmatter: name `smelt`; description first sentence the plain function (already
   "Consolidate one project's repository memory..."); keep the "not for new facts (/roar)" hint.
3. Edit live references in: AGENTS.md (3), README.md (3), STATE.md (2), memory/MEMORY.md (4),
   memory/SMELT.md, skills brood/lair/roar (+lair step 12 text and the `/hoard <repo>` suggestion
   line), skills/lair/references/session-lifecycle.md, skills-catalog.md (regenerate with
   `make skills-catalog`), scripts (migrate, census, trace-stats), tests (10 files above), tickets
   1346-1351 prose, memory/topics (5) only where they describe the current skill.
   Keep the Dragon names of Brood and Roar; capitalised "Hoard" becomes "Smelt".
4. Historical-name tables keep `hoard` and gain `smelt` (memory-recall regex, trace-stats
   MANDATED_SKILLS); lair step 12 reads both `memory/smelts/` and legacy `memory/hoards/`
   ledgers, or the git mv carries the ledger so only the new path is read (preferred: git mv).
5. Install: after merge, `bin/idh install skill smelt`; delete `~/.claude/skills/hoard` link on
   padme and doudou (and run `idh check`).
Stays untouched: memory/journal, conception, tickets/closed, memory/evidence, health/journal.jsonl,
report contents under memory/smelts/ (file names keep their dates and "hoard" words).
First failing test: none new. Existing tests that name hoard paths fail after the git mv and are
the red phase; edit them to green. Exit-criterion check goes in the PR body, not a permanent
guard: `git grep -n -i -w hoard -- . ':!memory/journal' ':!conception' ':!tickets/closed'
':!memory/smelts' ':!memory/evidence' ':!health'` must list only the declared historical-name
lines (census, trace-stats, migrate docstring). Then `make check` and `make check-skills-drift`.
Per-project tickets (file after the harness merge, cross-project rule): padme (rename
HOARD.md/hoards; has one) and nothing else strictly; JETP-observer, climate-finance-het,
arena/repos/agents have DREAM.md (migrate straight to SMELT.md, cheaper than two steps).
Decisions for the orchestrator: (a) exempt memory/evidence and health/ as history in the
exit criterion; (b) historical-name lines keep `hoard`; (c) exit criterion 3 narrows to
padme plus the three DREAM.md projects, others carry no store file.
